Game: Rent Day
Players: 2 to 8

Board:
  The board is a loop of spaces, starting at Go:
    | space           | kind       | color      | price | house price | rent | 1 house | 2 houses | 3 houses | 4 houses | with hotel | tax |
    | Go              | go         |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Mill Lane       | street     | brown      | 60    | 50          | 2    | 10      | 30       | 90       | 160      | 250        |     |
    | Treasury        | treasury   |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Ferry Row       | street     | brown      | 60    | 50          | 4    | 20      | 60       | 180      | 320      | 450        |     |
    | Income Tax      | tax        |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            | 200 |
    | North Station   | station    |            | 200   |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Ash Street      | street     | light blue | 100   | 50          | 6    | 30      | 90       | 270      | 400      | 550        |     |
    | Chance          | chance     |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Birch Street    | street     | light blue | 100   | 50          | 6    | 30      | 90       | 270      | 400      | 550        |     |
    | Cedar Avenue    | street     | light blue | 120   | 50          | 8    | 40      | 100      | 300      | 450      | 600        |     |
    | Jail            | jail       |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Dock Road       | street     | pink       | 140   | 100         | 10   | 50      | 150      | 450      | 625      | 750        |     |
    | Power Works     | utility    |            | 150   |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Quay Street     | street     | pink       | 140   | 100         | 10   | 50      | 150      | 450      | 625      | 750        |     |
    | Harbour Way     | street     | pink       | 160   | 100         | 12   | 60      | 180      | 500      | 700      | 900        |     |
    | East Station    | station    |            | 200   |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Rose Lane       | street     | orange     | 180   | 100         | 14   | 70      | 200      | 550      | 750      | 950        |     |
    | Treasury        | treasury   |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Lily Lane       | street     | orange     | 180   | 100         | 14   | 70      | 200      | 550      | 750      | 950        |     |
    | Iris Road       | street     | orange     | 200   | 100         | 16   | 80      | 220      | 600      | 800      | 1000       |     |
    | Free Parking    | parking    |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Market Square   | street     | red        | 220   | 150         | 18   | 90      | 250      | 700      | 875      | 1050       |     |
    | Chance          | chance     |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Guild Street    | street     | red        | 220   | 150         | 18   | 90      | 250      | 700      | 875      | 1050       |     |
    | Bell Square     | street     | red        | 240   | 150         | 20   | 100     | 300      | 750      | 925      | 1100       |     |
    | South Station   | station    |            | 200   |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Linden Walk     | street     | yellow     | 260   | 150         | 22   | 110     | 330      | 800      | 975      | 1150       |     |
    | Elm Walk        | street     | yellow     | 260   | 150         | 22   | 110     | 330      | 800      | 975      | 1150       |     |
    | Pump House      | utility    |            | 150   |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Oak Gardens     | street     | yellow     | 280   | 150         | 24   | 120     | 360      | 850      | 1025     | 1200       |     |
    | Go To Jail      | go to jail |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Crown Row       | street     | green      | 300   | 200         | 26   | 130     | 390      | 900      | 1100     | 1275       |     |
    | Bishop's Row    | street     | green      | 300   | 200         | 26   | 130     | 390      | 900      | 1100     | 1275       |     |
    | Treasury        | treasury   |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Castle Row      | street     | green      | 320   | 200         | 28   | 150     | 450      | 1000     | 1200     | 1400       |     |
    | West Station    | station    |            | 200   |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Chance          | chance     |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            |     |
    | Harbour Heights | street     | dark blue  | 350   | 200         | 35   | 175     | 500      | 1100     | 1300     | 1500       |     |
    | Luxury Tax      | tax        |            |       |             |      |         |          |          |          |            | 100 |
    | The Promenade   | street     | dark blue  | 400   | 200         | 50   | 200     | 600      | 1400     | 1700     | 2000       |     |
  Each player has a piece that starts on Go.
  Each player has 1500 money that everyone can see.
  Players pay with money.
  There are two six-sided dice.
  Spaces can have houses and a hotel.
  The bank has 32 houses and 12 hotels.
  Players can be in jail.
  Players can have jail turns.

Rent:
  A street's rent depends on its houses and hotel.
  A street in a full set with no buildings has double rent.
  A station's rent is 25, 50, 100 or 200 when its owner has 1, 2, 3 or 4 stations.
  A utility's rent is 4 times the roll, or 10 times when its owner has both.

Phase: playing
  Hint: Roll the dice, then buy, build, or end your turn. A double rolls again.
  Players take turns.
  A player may roll the dice.
    Only if they are not in jail.
    Only if they have not rolled for a double this turn.
    Only if one of:
      they have not rolled this turn
      they rolled a double
    Then:
      Roll the dice.
      If they have rolled fewer than 3 doubles this turn, their piece moves forward by the roll.
  A player may pay to leave jail.
    Only if they are in jail.
    Only if they have not rolled this turn.
    Only if they have at least 50 money.
    Then:
      They pay 50.
      They are not in jail.
      Their jail turns go back to 0.
  A player may roll for a double.
    Only if they are in jail.
    Only if they have not rolled this turn.
    Then:
      Roll the dice.
      If they rolled a double, they are not in jail.
      If they are in jail, they gain 1 jail turn.
      If they are not in jail, their jail turns go back to 0.
      If they are not in jail, their piece moves forward by the roll.
  A player may buy the space they are on.
    Only if they have rolled this turn.
    Only if it has a price.
    Only if no one owns it.
    Only if they have at least its price in money.
    Then:
      They pay its price.
      They own it.
  A player may build a house on a street they own.
    Only if they own every street of its color.
    Only if it has no hotel.
    Only if no street of its color has fewer buildings.
    Only if they have at least its house price in money.
    Only if one of:
      it has fewer than 4 houses
      the bank has a hotel
    Only if one of:
      it has 4 houses
      the bank has a house
    Then:
      They pay its house price.
      If it has 4 houses, it gets a hotel from the bank.
      If it has a hotel, its houses go back to the bank.
      If it has no hotel, it gets a house from the bank.
  A player may end their turn.
    Only if they have rolled this turn.
    Only if one of:
      they did not roll a double
      they are in jail
      they have rolled for a double this turn
  When a player has rolled 3 doubles this turn:
    Only if they are not in jail.
    Their piece goes straight to Jail.
    They are in jail.
  When a player lands on a go to jail space:
    Their piece goes straight to Jail.
    They are in jail.
  When a player has 3 jail turns:
    They pay 50.
    They are not in jail.
    Their jail turns go back to 0.
    Their piece moves forward by the roll.
  When a piece passes Go:
    Its player gets 200 money.
  When a player lands on a space someone else owns:
    They pay its rent to its owner.
  When a player lands on a tax space:
    They pay its tax.
  When a player has less than 0 money:
    They are out.
    Their houses go back to the bank.
    Their hotels go back to the bank.
    Their spaces go back to the bank.
  After a player ends their turn, the turn passes to the left.

End:
  The game ends when one player is left.
  That player wins.

Example: landing on someone else's street pays them rent
  Given p1 owns Rose Lane
  And p0 is on Cedar Avenue
  And the next roll is 3 and 4
  When p0 rolls the dice
  Then p0 is on Rose Lane
  And p0 has 1486 money
  And p1 has 1514 money

Example: a player can buy the street they land on
  Given p0 is on Cedar Avenue
  And the next roll is 3 and 4
  When p0 rolls the dice
  And p0 buys the space they are on
  Then it is accepted
  And p0 owns Rose Lane
  And p0 has 1320 money

Example: you cannot buy before rolling
  Given p0 is on Rose Lane
  When p0 buys the space they are on
  Then it is rejected because "they have rolled this turn"

Example: you cannot buy a space that has no price
  Given p0 is on Go
  And the next roll is 3 and 4
  When p0 rolls the dice
  And p0 buys the space they are on
  Then it is rejected because "it has a price"

Example: you cannot buy a space someone owns
  Given p1 owns Rose Lane
  And p0 is on Cedar Avenue
  And the next roll is 3 and 4
  When p0 rolls the dice
  And p0 buys the space they are on
  Then it is rejected because "no one owns it"

Example: you cannot buy without enough money
  Given p0 has 100 money
  And p0 is on Cedar Avenue
  And the next roll is 3 and 4
  When p0 rolls the dice
  And p0 buys the space they are on
  Then it is rejected because "they have at least its price in money"

Example: you cannot roll twice in one turn
  Given p0 is on Go
  And the next roll is 1 and 2
  When p0 rolls the dice
  And p0 rolls the dice
  Then it is rejected because "they have not rolled this turn or they rolled a double"

Example: you cannot end your turn before rolling
  When p0 ends their turn
  Then it is rejected because "they have rolled this turn"

